From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: configure: no profile-use flag in cross builds without a profile task

With --enable-optimizations, a cross build runs no profile task (009), so
the profile-guided build step compiles with the profile-use flag but no
profile exists. GCC only warns about the missing data; clang stops on the
missing profile file (code.profclangd). Leave the flag empty then.

Measured on an AArch64 ILP32 OpenWrt One with GCC 14.3 (-Os, LTO):
without the flag the speed is the same (geometric mean of 9 benchmarks
+0.3%).

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -2177,6 +2177,10 @@
     ;;
 esac
 
+# A cross build runs no profile task (PROFILE_TASK is empty), so there is no profile to use: GCC
+# would only warn about the missing data, clang stops on the missing profile file.
+AS_IF([test "x$cross_compiling" = xyes -a -z "$PROFILE_TASK"], [PGO_PROF_USE_FLAG=""])
+
 # BOLT optimization. Always configured after PGO since it always runs after PGO.
 Py_BOLT='false'
 AC_MSG_CHECKING([for --enable-bolt])
